--
N5008 [temp.deduct.general]/8: type deduction fails when substituting the
deduced arguments forms an invalid type, e.g. a reference to void.  The
shape is libstdc++'s range-access customization points
(bits/iterator_concepts.h): the poison pills `void begin(auto &) = delete'
make `begin(t)' a void expression for a built-in array, and the
`__adl_begin' concept's `__decay_copy(begin(__t))' must then fail to
deduce `_Tp &&' rather than instantiate `_Decay_copy::operator()<void>',
whose parameter cannot be declared ("symbol '__t' is unknown", the body
dropped -- audit residue item 4, round 162: every std::ranges algorithm
over an array).  Fixed in round 163.
